- Files are preferred over inline code dumps for anything substantial.
- He cares about deliverable craft. Read existing files before editing; match the style that's there.
- The Bobiverse metaphor is canon: Garfield (Cursor/this assistant) is the implementer Bob. Bill (the assistant on qiklog.com later) is the interview twin. Reference is fine, don't overdo it.

## Definition of done for a feature

1. Code compiles with zero warnings (warnings are errors here).
2. Unit tests cover the happy path and at least one failure case.
3. Public APIs have XML doc comments.
4. `docker compose up` still works end-to-end.
5. The README quickstart still demonstrates the system correctly.

## When in doubt

- Smaller changes are better than larger ones.
- Working code is better than clever code.
- Boring is better than novel.
- Ask before adding a NuGet dependency.
